{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794391107,"nonce":"XVfAKANLfAQ03VSs/p8PKdZeRcA=","title":"GPU animation P6: resize without a rebuild, a stretched last frame, and snapshot transitions","message":"Part of the GPU-deferral plan (umbrella issue). 6a closes the point of 4f48675. 6b and 6c depend on P2.\n\n**6a: relayout, not rebuild.** The `Resized` handler sets `needs_rebuild` and `needs_relayout`; the next frame runs the app's build closure and replaces the whole `RenderTree` (a full build, not `incremental_update`), which drops FLIP, visual and layout animations on the old tree and trips `tree_owner_changed`, which drains the layer textures. A resize changes the viewport, not the structure. Track whether the build read the window size, or give the build a viewport signal to bind to.\n\n**6b: stretch the last frame.** While relayout catches up, draw the last frame scaled. Obstacles found: `ensure_static_layer` reallocates the texture on a size change and drops the pixels; `blit_static_layer_into` uses `copy_texture_to_texture` with the layer's own extent and cannot scale; the swapchain contents are undefined after `configure`. So copy the old static layer before reallocation and add a scaling quad pass. Glass backbuffers and custom passes resize on the first new-size frame.\n\n**6c: snapshot transitions.** Page transitions and shared-element effects render the old and new states to textures and animate between them. The standard form is CSS View Transitions (`view-transition-name`, `::view-transition-old()` and `::view-transition-new()`), built on the layer textures and tracks from P2. Optional and last.\n\n**API.** CSS (View Transitions) and an internal viewport signal. No Rust animation API.\n\nAcceptance: a live resize runs the build closure only when it reads the window size; no black or undefined frame during resize; FLIP and visual animations survive a resize.","files":null}]}